<title>ISRAEL: Israeli provident funds prefer Koor.</title>
<headline>Israeli provident funds prefer Koor.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koor Industries Ltd is the most popular stock with Israel's provident funds, a report by Meitav Investments and Securities said.</p>
<p>At mid-year the five biggest provident fund managers held shares in Koor worth a total of 438 million shekels, Meitav said.</p>
<p>After Koor the most popular shares are I.D.B Development Corp, Discount Investment Corp Ltd, I.D.B. Holdings and Israel Chemicals Ltd.</p>
<p>The five biggest provident fund managers, which are the five biggest commercial banks in Israel, at mid-year held assets totalling 73 billion shekels. These banks manage 65 percent of the total assets of Israeli provident funds.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
